#: mintcare/tweaks.py:225
msgid ""
"Google's BBR algorithm with the fq qdisc. Higher throughput and lower "
"latency on most connections, especially lossy Wi-Fi."
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:234
msgid "Network stack tuning"
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:235
msgid ""
"TCP Fast Open, MTU probing and larger socket buffers (16 MB) for fast links."
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:245
msgid "Encrypted DNS (Cloudflare + Quad9)"
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:246
msgid ""
"Use 1.1.1.1 and 9.9.9.9 with opportunistic DNS-over-TLS through systemd-"
"resolved. Faster lookups and more privacy than many ISP resolvers."
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:263
msgid "Compressed RAM swap (zram)"
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:264
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Adds a zstd-compressed swap device in RAM (50% of memory). Keeps the desktop "
"responsive under memory pressure and reduces SSD writes."
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:280
msgid "Low swappiness (disk swap only)"
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:281
msgid ""
"Prefer RAM over a swap file/partition (swappiness 10, cache pressure 50). "
"Use this instead of zram if you keep plain disk swap."
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:286
msgid "Smoother disk writeback"
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:287
msgid ""
"Flush dirty pages earlier (64 MB background / 256 MB max) so large copies to "
"USB sticks don't stall the desktop."
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:294
msgid "Weekly SSD TRIM"
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:295
msgid ""
"Enable fstrim.timer so SSDs are trimmed weekly, keeping write speeds up."
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:301
msgid "Cap system logs at 200 MB"
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:302
msgid ""
"Limit the systemd journal to 200 MB and 1 month so logs never fill the disk."
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:316
msgid "Automatic old-kernel/orphan removal"
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:317
msgid ""
"Turn on Mint Update's weekly automation that removes obsolete kernels and "
"orphaned packages."
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:326 mintcare/tweaks.py:339 mintcare/tweaks.py:397
msgid "Boot & Services"
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:326
msgid "Faster shutdown"
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:327
msgid ""
"Wait at most 10 s (instead of 90 s) for hung services when shutting down."
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:339
msgid "Skip 'wait for network' at boot"
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:340
msgid ""
"Disable NetworkManager-wait-online, which can add several seconds to boot. "
"Leave this off if you mount network shares (NFS/SMB) in /etc/fstab."
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:349
msgid "Enable the firewall: block all incoming connections, allow outgoing."
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:358
msgid "Automatic updates"
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:359
msgid ""
"Let Mint Update install updates automatically in the background (Timeshift "
"snapshot recommended)."
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:366
msgid "CPU microcode updates"
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:367
msgid ""
"Install the vendor microcode package: fixes CPU bugs and security issues."
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:374
msgid "Best I/O scheduler per drive"
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:375
msgid ""
"NVMe: none · SATA SSD: mq-deadline · hard drives: BFQ. BFQ keeps the desktop "
"responsive while a hard drive is busy copying or indexing."
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:397
msgid "Faster boot menu (GRUB)"
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:398
msgid ""
"After a crash or power cut Ubuntu-based systems show the GRUB menu for 30 s. "
"This cuts that to 5 s and keeps the normal menu short (2 s, or 3 s when dual-"
"booting). Uses a drop-in file; /etc/default/grub is not edited and grub.cfg "
"is backed up first."
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:409 mintcare/tweaks.py:414 mintcare/tweaks.py:424
#: mintcare/tweaks.py:440 mintcare/tweaks.py:447 mintcare/tweaks.py:457
#: mintcare/tweaks.py:559
msgid "Gaming"
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:409
msgid "Raise vm.max_map_count"
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:410
msgid ""
"Raise the memory-map limit to SteamOS's value. Prevents crashes in some "
"Proton/Steam games (e.g. CS2, Hogwarts Legacy)."
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:414
msgid "Feral GameMode"
msgstr ""

#: mintcare/tweaks.py:415
msgid ""
"Temporarily boosts CPU/GPU performance while a game runs. Also adds you to "
